 *   **Time Complexity**: Linear with respect to the number of voxels processed per slice [S1, unofficial]. Total wall-clock time is significantly reduced compared to serial execution; for a ~2.2M grid dataset, time reduced from ~20 min to ~90 s [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Memory Complexity**: $O(S)$, where $S$ is the size of a single slice (or two slices) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance**: Tested on SUN4 (2 processors), SGI Challenge (8 processors), and KSR1 (8 processors); timings include I/O overhead [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths**: Handles huge datasets; machine-independent parallel execution; supports irregular grids [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations**: Requires specific grid orientation (k-slice); serialization bottleneck during output writing; platform-specific process creation (`sproc` vs `fork`) [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Performance**: Tested on SUN4 (2 processors), SGI Challenge (8 processors), and KSR1 (8 processors); timings include I/O overhead [S1, unofficial]. On an nCUBE 2, a 10x10x10 dataset took 0.06 s local time and 0.055 s host communication time with 1 processor, while a 66x66x50 dataset took 0.002 s local time and 4.05 s host communication time with 64 processors [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths**: Handles huge datasets; machine-independent parallel execution; supports irregular grids [S1, unofficial]. Object-space methods are inherently parallel and simpler to parallelize than image-space methods [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations**: Requires specific grid orientation (k-slice); serialization bottleneck during output writing; platform-specific process creation (`sproc` vs `fork`) [S1, unofficial]. The isosurface composition phase is a significant communications bottleneck because it is entirely sequential, causing total communication time to increase as processor count increases [S2, unofficial]. Load imbalance occurs because different hypercube dimensions result in different data distributions, causing processors with small isosurface portions to wait for those with larger portions [S2, unofficial].
 
